note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note om/tls/sha2.om: SHA-256, SHA-384, SHA-512 (FIPS 180-4) streaming, as an OM-2 library unit
note (no om2 line, no main, no globals). Module code SH; functions sha2_*, sha256_*, sha384_*, sha512_*.
note
note API
note   sha256_init c edit ulong *            c: 40 ulong cells (caller owns all state)
note   sha256_update c edit ulong * m view uchar *   any length, any chunking
note   sha256_final c edit ulong * o edit uchar *    writes 32 bytes (o shorter traps 3)
note   sha384_* / sha512_* the same; final writes 48 / 64 bytes
note   sha2_copy d edit ulong * s view ulong *       copies len s cells (a context snapshot)
note   sha2_digest alg ulong m view uchar * o edit uchar * to ulong
note     alg 256|384|512: one-shot digest into o, returns 32|48|64; any other alg returns 0, writes nothing
note After final the context is spent (its state cells hold the last chaining value); init it again.
note A context initialised for one algorithm must be used with that algorithm's update/final; the
note common code reads the algorithm from cell 9, so sha256_update on a sha512 context hashes SHA-512.
note
note Context cells: 0..7 chaining value H (32-bit words zero-extended for SHA-256), 8 = bytes absorbed
note mod 2^64, 9 = algorithm (256, 384, 512), 16..31 = pending block bytes packed big-endian (byte i
note in cell 16 + i/8, bits 56 - 8*(i mod 8)), 10..15 and 32..39 = 0.
note Constant time: every branch, loop count and index depends only on lengths and the algorithm,
note never on message or state bytes. Local schedule/state/padding arrays are zeroed before return
note (HMAC keys pass through them). omc emits plain AArch64; MUL/ADD/EOR/ROR/shift data-independent.
note Message length: any length below 2^64 bytes; update cuts its input into runs of 2^25 bytes so no
note loop passes 2^20 times (a rolled for traps 4 after 10^6 passes; the while bound 999999 of runs
note allows inputs up to 999999 * 32 MiB per update call).

note K{256}[0..64): first 32 bits of the fractional parts of the cube roots of the first 64 primes
note (FIPS 180-4 4.2.2). Same values as om/sha256/sha256-om2.om; recomputed with Wolfram:
note IntegerString[Floor[FractionalPart[N[CubeRoot[Prime[i]],60]]*2^32],16,8] for i = 1..64.
fn sha2_k256 k edit uint 64 to void
put k 0 0x428a2f98
put k 1 0x71374491
put k 2 0xb5c0fbcf
put k 3 0xe9b5dba5
put k 4 0x3956c25b
